A||N||7||RiceBurner515||2 10" Subs in console?||||1||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||12-11-2000||12:33 AM||||me and my friend were thinking about putting 2 10's in my console/armrest and just take out the whole console and make a custom box to put in place of it....would this work, anyone try it b4?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RiceBurner515||12-11-2000||12:36 AM||||o yea, one would be in the armrest facing up, slightly toward the front window and the other where the "glove compartment" is facing the window.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-11-2000||02:20 AM||||You will have a hard time fitting 2 10's. Each 10 is going to need .6 to .7 cubic inches of space. The 10 where the glove box is can be done. (moving ECM to behind driver seat gains more room) But the other one will be difficultDue to the speaker depth. Most 10's run close to 5" deep, so the armrest one will raise the arm rest that high. You cannot sink it in due to shifting cables and harness'. If you raise it up 5" you'll be cutting into the room required for the glovebox position. One member of our club is in the process of installing 2 10's like Fierosounds, (behind the seats cutting into the firewall) and putting a single 10 in the glovebox spot. He'll have 3 10's and driving them mono at 200W each.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Stoic||12-11-2000||08:05 AM||||I have a 10" sony explode mounted under the passenger side dash.  I had it professionally done.  I t fits in perfect, although it is not 100% sealed, it sounds good and you can't even tell its there unless you lean right down in and look up.  If I had a scanner I'd show a pic.  But they did a really nice job on it for me.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||12-11-2000||03:27 PM||||Yea it can be done. I did it in my first fiero. It will cost about $900-1300 to do you will need to move the ECM I moved mine up  where the factory sub goes (custom wireing harness $200) my box was black fiberglass built buy East coast audio and had about .75 cu ft of space (per sub) i used tow 10" hollywood DVC's and a US-Amps VLX-50 to run them. I can have a similar box built (does extent to the roof and blocks usage on the sunroof) for $1000 and make a wireing harness for the ECM for $200 (inclides a harness for the port by the lighter to be mounted under dash) i could also load the box with two Infinity aluminum cone subs (1000 watts each) for $500 more and a rockford bd1000a1 for another $550.<P><BR>all in all the hollywoods cracked my windshield seal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||12-11-2000||10:51 PM||||any pics of this install?<P>Josh||||reg||5
Z||000006||RiceBurner515||12-12-2000||02:50 PM||||no pics yet sorry, i haven't done it yet, i hopefully will be doing it some time this week and i will definitely post pics up for you guys...how would i move the ECM to behind the driver's side seat...? do i just move it and bolt it up or something? i don't need any harnesses right? hope not....||||reg||1
